  "notes": [
    "The MI300X rigs differ from each other only in checkpoint, so two of them are an A/B pair when both reports name the same container image and vLLM version \u2014 never otherwise, since the nightly image drifts daily. Nothing outside them serves on AMD, so these figures must not be differenced against a TPU or EC2 rig and read as a hardware result.",
    "Prefix caching is enabled (vLLM's default) and was left on, because that is how the rig actually serves. Each repeat uses a different bench seed so repeats are independent samples rather than replays into a warm cache, but the random dataset still shares some prefixes within a run, so prefill-bound cells are optimistic relative to unique traffic.",
    "The load generator ran on the same host as the server, in a container with no GPU device attached. It costs host CPU, not card time."
  ]
